1
00:00:02,750 --> 00:00:03,790
Hey.

2
00:00:03,960 --> 00:00:07,920
I just got my teacher evaluations. Check out what this one student wrote.

3
00:00:08,090 --> 00:00:12,340
"I loved Dr. Geller's class. Mind-blowing lectures.

4
00:00:12,510 --> 00:00:17,720
Dr. Geller, you are definitely the hottie of the Paleontology Department."

5
00:00:19,220 --> 00:00:21,020
Ah, "Hotties of the Paleontology Department."

6
00:00:21,180 --> 00:00:23,430
There's a big-selling calendar, huh?

7
00:00:24,850 --> 00:00:25,890
Who wrote it?

8
00:00:26,060 --> 00:00:28,650
I wish I knew, but the evaluations are all anonymous.

9
00:00:28,860 --> 00:00:30,900
Do you still have their final exams?

10
00:00:28,860 --> 00:00:30,900
Yeah.

11
00:00:31,110 --> 00:00:35,450
Match the evaluation to the exam with the same handwriting and there's your admirer.

12
00:00:37,370 --> 00:00:40,080
A hot girl's at stake and all of a sudden he's Rain Man.

13
00:00:41,830 --> 00:00:45,830
Hey, wait a minute, wait a minute. Why are we so sure that this is a girl?

14
00:00:50,090 --> 00:00:51,500
It's a girl.

15
00:00:52,880 --> 00:00:54,420
Anyway, it wouldn't matter, okay?

16
00:00:54,590 --> 00:00:58,470
Because I'm a teacher. She's a student.

17
00:00:54,590 --> 00:00:58,470
Oh, is that against the rules?

18
00:00:58,640 --> 00:01:00,260
No, but it is frowned upon.

19
00:00:58,640 --> 00:01:00,260
I see.

20
00:01:00,430 --> 00:01:02,190
Besides, there's a big age difference.

21
00:01:02,190 --> 00:01:04,140
Think of it like this. When you're 90...

22
00:01:04,310 --> 00:01:05,980
I know, when I'm 90, she'll be 80...

23
00:01:06,140 --> 00:01:08,310
and it won't seem like such a big difference.

24
00:01:09,770 --> 00:01:12,230
No, that's not what I was gonna say at all.

25
00:01:13,940 --> 00:01:15,780
What I was gonna say is when you're 90...

26
00:01:15,950 --> 00:01:19,620
you'll still have the memory of what it was like to be with a 20-year-old.

27
00:01:59,990 --> 00:02:03,990
Chandler, you know that girl you went to college with who became a movie director?

28
00:02:04,160 --> 00:02:07,540
Oh, yeah, Dana Keystone. She was in my movement class.

29
00:02:08,160 --> 00:02:09,790
What's a movement class?

30
00:02:09,960 --> 00:02:13,340
It's Chandler's way of pretending he didn't take mime.

31
00:02:13,880 --> 00:02:17,670
Listen, anyway, she's directing the new Al Pacino movie.

32
00:02:17,840 --> 00:02:21,300
You gotta get me an audition.

33
00:02:17,840 --> 00:02:21,300
Oh. I haven't talked to her in like 10 years.

34
00:02:21,470 --> 00:02:24,430
Oh, no, no, no. Please, Chandler, I would owe you so much.

35
00:02:24,600 --> 00:02:27,810
You do owe me so much. You owe me 3400...

36
00:02:27,980 --> 00:02:31,650
Hey, hey, dude. Why you changing the subject? What?

37
00:02:31,810 --> 00:02:34,730
Will you make the call or what?

38
00:02:31,810 --> 00:02:34,730
Okay, I'll try.

39
00:02:34,900 --> 00:02:36,650
All right. Thanks, you're the best.

40
00:02:36,820 --> 00:02:40,070
The last day of auditions is Thursday, so I gotta get in by Thursday.

41
00:02:40,240 --> 00:02:43,120
Just remember Thursday. Thursday. Can you remember Thursday?

42
00:02:44,370 --> 00:02:45,530
Yeah, so Tuesday?

43
00:02:47,410 --> 00:02:51,330
Thursday. Look, if you need help remembering, just think of it like this.

44
00:02:51,500 --> 00:02:54,380
The third day. All right? Monday, one day.

45
00:02:54,540 --> 00:02:56,590
Tuesday, two day.

46
00:02:56,750 --> 00:03:00,470
Wednesday, when, huh, what day? Thursday.

47
00:03:00,630 --> 00:03:03,220
The third day, okay?

48
00:03:04,470 --> 00:03:05,930
Thank you.

49
00:03:04,470 --> 00:03:05,930
Okay.

50
00:03:07,810 --> 00:03:11,310
Hey, Mon, I'm gonna check my messages.

51
00:03:07,810 --> 00:03:11,310
You just thought of that in there?

52
00:03:11,480 --> 00:03:14,350
Sure, you know, nature called. She wants to see who else did.

53
00:03:16,650 --> 00:03:18,360
Hello?

54
00:03:18,650 --> 00:03:19,900
Uh...

55
00:03:20,070 --> 00:03:21,280
Rachel.

56
00:03:21,450 --> 00:03:23,950
You guys, someone is in our apartment. Call the cops.

57
00:03:24,120 --> 00:03:26,410
You're on the phone.

58
00:03:26,660 --> 00:03:28,580
Oh, my God.

59
00:03:26,660 --> 00:03:28,580
What?

60
00:03:28,750 --> 00:03:31,830
Oh, my God. Thank you. That was the Fire Department.

61
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:35,460
There was a fire at our place.

62
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:35,460
Oh, my God. How bad was it?

63
00:03:35,630 --> 00:03:38,750
He didn't say, but it was a fire. I'm guessing not very good.

64
00:03:38,920 --> 00:03:41,170
Come on, we gotta go.

65
00:03:38,920 --> 00:03:41,170
Phoebe, come on.

66
00:03:43,340 --> 00:03:45,720
What are you smiling about? What is so funny?

67
00:03:45,890 --> 00:03:50,470
The part I wanna audition for is a fireman. This is so meant to be.

68
00:03:58,940 --> 00:04:03,450
Wow. Looks like you were very generous with your grades this semester.

69
00:04:09,160 --> 00:04:11,620
Professor Geller?

70
00:04:09,160 --> 00:04:11,620
Yeah? Huh?

71
00:04:12,370 --> 00:04:14,500
I wanted to say how much I enjoyed your class.

72
00:04:14,670 --> 00:04:17,540
Oh, thank you. Thanks very much. Ow.

73
00:04:18,710 --> 00:04:22,210
I'm a little embarrassed about calling you a hottie on my evaluation.

74
00:04:22,840 --> 00:04:24,630
That was you?

75
00:04:22,840 --> 00:04:24,630
Yeah.

76
00:04:24,800 --> 00:04:28,550
I felt a little weird about it. You're a teacher. I'm a student.

77
00:04:30,100 --> 00:04:32,600
But would you maybe wanna go out with me sometime?

78
00:04:32,770 --> 00:04:35,980
Oh, I... Heh. I don't think that would be the best idea.

79
00:04:36,150 --> 00:04:40,110
Oh, because I was thinking, um, the semester's over.

80
00:04:40,280 --> 00:04:42,940
You're not my teacher anymore.

81
00:04:40,280 --> 00:04:42,940
What time?

82
00:04:45,280 --> 00:04:49,370
Oh, you know what? Forget it. I see you already gave me an A.

83
00:04:50,990 --> 00:04:53,950
Gotcha.

84
00:04:50,990 --> 00:04:53,950
I'm kidding. Ha-ha-ha.

85
00:04:54,160 --> 00:04:55,710
Oh. Ha-ha-ha.

86
00:04:54,160 --> 00:04:55,710
Ha-ha-ha.

87
00:04:55,870 --> 00:04:58,210
So seriously, what time?

88
00:05:02,920 --> 00:05:05,760
Coming through. Oh. Coming through. Oh. Hello. Hi.

89
00:05:06,340 --> 00:05:08,720
No, right. Coming through.

90
00:05:08,890 --> 00:05:10,680
Oh.

91
00:05:08,890 --> 00:05:10,680
Okay. Well, it's not so bad.

92
00:05:10,850 --> 00:05:12,970
Most of the damage was contained to the bedrooms.

93
00:05:13,140 --> 00:05:14,180
Oh, my God.

94
00:05:14,350 --> 00:05:17,560
Hey, buddy, you think I could borrow your uniform this Thursday?

95
00:05:18,440 --> 00:05:21,360
Excuse me?

96
00:05:18,440 --> 00:05:21,360
Joey. He's working.

97
00:05:21,820 --> 00:05:24,030
You would look good in that.

98
00:05:25,190 --> 00:05:28,610
Uh-oh. How bad is it?

99
00:05:25,190 --> 00:05:28,610
Oh, it's bad, it's really bad.

100
00:05:28,780 --> 00:05:34,410
The only thing that isn't burned is an ax, which I do not remember buying.

101
00:05:34,620 --> 00:05:36,830
How's your room, Rach?

102
00:05:34,620 --> 00:05:36,830
Everything's ruined.

103
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:39,540
My bed, my clothes. Look at my favorite blue sweater.

104
00:05:39,710 --> 00:05:40,750
Isn't that mine?

105
00:05:41,840 --> 00:05:44,420
Fine. I'm sorry for your loss.

106
00:05:46,220 --> 00:05:48,510
You're not gonna be able to live here for a while.

107
00:05:48,680 --> 00:05:51,760
You ladies have a place to stay?

108
00:05:48,680 --> 00:05:51,760
Oh. Wow.

109
00:05:51,930 --> 00:05:55,270
Okay, look, pal...

110
00:05:55,430 --> 00:05:58,390
I am not in the mood to be hit on right now.

111
00:05:58,560 --> 00:06:01,770
But if you give me your number, I will call you some other time.

112
00:06:04,150 --> 00:06:06,490
Yes, they can stay with us.

113
00:06:06,650 --> 00:06:09,280
Have you figured out what started the fire, Mr. Fireman?

114
00:06:10,620 --> 00:06:12,740
Well, uh, do either of you smoke?

115
00:06:12,910 --> 00:06:13,950
No, not usually.

116
00:06:14,120 --> 00:06:16,410
But yeah, I could use one now. Thanks.

117
00:06:14,120 --> 00:06:16,410
No, no.

118
00:06:16,580 --> 00:06:20,830
Do you light candles, burn incense?

119
00:06:16,580 --> 00:06:20,830
Yes, I do all the time. I love them.

120
00:06:22,590 --> 00:06:24,800
Oh, my God, I did it. It's me, it's me.

121
00:06:24,960 --> 00:06:27,710
I burned down the house. I burned down the house!

122
00:06:27,880 --> 00:06:31,260
Okay, Phoebe, calm down. There's no need to place blame. Okay?

123
00:06:31,430 --> 00:06:34,050
I warned her about those candles.

124
00:06:37,430 --> 00:06:40,520
It's great to catch up. I can't believe how long it's been.

125
00:06:40,690 --> 00:06:43,230
Hey, Chandler, is that?

126
00:06:45,530 --> 00:06:48,150
Oh, that's great. Good for you.

127
00:06:45,530 --> 00:06:48,150
So, hey, hey, is it?

128
00:06:50,700 --> 00:06:53,820
Okay, so, yeah, maybe we can get together, um...

129
00:06:59,870 --> 00:07:01,750
Can you hold on for one second, please?

130
00:07:02,210 --> 00:07:03,460
What?

131
00:07:03,630 --> 00:07:06,500
When you're off the phone, you wanna get a pizza?

132
00:07:07,260 --> 00:07:08,920
Hi, I'm back.

133
00:07:09,470 --> 00:07:14,140
Yeah, that sounds great. Okay, well, we'll do it then. Okay, bye.

134
00:07:16,600 --> 00:07:20,100
Hey, listen, so when's my audition? I know it's Thursday, but what time?

135
00:07:21,560 --> 00:07:23,440
Hi. We didn't get to the audition.

136
00:07:23,600 --> 00:07:26,310
I'm gonna take her to coffee and do it then.

137
00:07:23,600 --> 00:07:26,310
Ah.

138
00:07:26,480 --> 00:07:29,110
Wow, so now you're going on a date with this girl?

139
00:07:29,280 --> 00:07:31,450
Not a date. I haven't talked to her in 10 years.

140
00:07:31,610 --> 00:07:35,240
You can't call somebody you haven't talked to in 10 years and ask for a favor.

141
00:07:35,410 --> 00:07:37,910
There are rules, you know? You gotta put in some time.

142
00:07:38,080 --> 00:07:39,330
You're right, I'm sorry.

143
00:07:39,500 --> 00:07:43,000
It's not like you're going out with an ex.

144
00:07:39,500 --> 00:07:43,000
No, we only went out once.

145
00:07:43,170 --> 00:07:45,040
You dated her?

146
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:47,710
Not once.

147
00:07:48,920 --> 00:07:53,340
Great. Why don't I just go out with an ex, you know, and do Joey a favor?

148
00:07:53,510 --> 00:07:56,720
Hey, you wanna do Joey a favor? Maybe you go out with Joey.

149
00:08:05,310 --> 00:08:07,980
Oh. That's great. My friend Joey's in the movie business.

150
00:08:08,150 --> 00:08:11,570
Mm. You know who I ran into from school? Howie.

151
00:08:11,780 --> 00:08:14,570
Hmm. My friend's name is Joey.

152
00:08:11,780 --> 00:08:14,570
Heh.

153
00:08:14,740 --> 00:08:17,160
Apparently, Howie's editing now.

154
00:08:17,330 --> 00:08:21,620
Yeah, he calls me up and asks me if he can edit my new movie.

155
00:08:21,790 --> 00:08:23,160
Heh. Can you believe that?

156
00:08:23,330 --> 00:08:26,080
You know, I haven't spoken to him in, what, 10 years...

157
00:08:26,250 --> 00:08:29,090
and he asks me for a favor?

158
00:08:31,460 --> 00:08:34,510
Yeah, I've always hated that Howie.

159
00:08:34,680 --> 00:08:37,050
No "How you doing?" Heh.

160
00:08:37,220 --> 00:08:40,390
Man, I mean, not even a cup of coffee first.

161
00:08:40,560 --> 00:08:42,390
Heh. The nerve, huh?

162
00:08:40,560 --> 00:08:42,390
Yeah.

163
00:08:42,560 --> 00:08:43,930
Refill?

164
00:08:45,730 --> 00:08:48,480
Now, this is last-minute, so I want to apologize for the mess.

165
00:08:48,650 --> 00:08:51,150
Oh.

166
00:08:48,650 --> 00:08:51,150
Who cares?

167
00:08:53,780 --> 00:08:55,400
Oh, my God.

168
00:08:55,570 --> 00:08:57,780
It sure didn't look this way when I lived here.

169
00:08:57,950 --> 00:08:59,410
I know.

170
00:09:01,240 --> 00:09:02,580
There's one problem, though.

171
00:09:02,750 --> 00:09:06,540
There's only room for one, so I guess one of you will have to stay at Joey's.

172
00:09:06,710 --> 00:09:10,840
Well, since the fire was kind of my fault, I guess you should get to stay here.

173
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:12,380
Hey, hey, hey, now.

174
00:09:12,550 --> 00:09:15,670
This was no one's fault, Pheebs, okay? It was an accident.

175
00:09:15,840 --> 00:09:17,970
It was my fault. You should get the nice room.

176
00:09:18,140 --> 00:09:20,470
Okay. Whoo!

177
00:09:20,640 --> 00:09:22,890
So, Rach, you're the first guest at Hotel Monica.

178
00:09:23,060 --> 00:09:24,100
Hotel Monica.

179
00:09:24,270 --> 00:09:26,390
Just tell me how you like your eggs.

180
00:09:26,560 --> 00:09:28,650
I thought I'd bring them to you, you know, in bed.

181
00:09:28,810 --> 00:09:30,400
Aw.

182
00:09:28,810 --> 00:09:30,400
You've been through so much.

183
00:09:30,570 --> 00:09:31,610
I have.

184
00:09:33,320 --> 00:09:36,400
This right here is where I keep the pizza.

185
00:09:37,610 --> 00:09:39,700
And that's where the napkin is.

186
00:09:40,700 --> 00:09:43,950
What's that smell?

187
00:09:40,700 --> 00:09:43,950
I know. I don't...

188
00:09:47,250 --> 00:09:51,920
Oh, please, it was such a big class. You never even noticed me.

189
00:09:52,090 --> 00:09:56,380
What? Of course I did. You sat next to Sleepy Sleeperson.

190
00:09:56,550 --> 00:09:57,590
Who?

191
00:09:57,760 --> 00:10:00,260
Oh. I had trouble remembering everyone's names...

192
00:10:00,430 --> 00:10:01,890
so I came up with nicknames.

193
00:10:02,050 --> 00:10:06,270
Like the guy on the other side of you was Smelly von Brown-Shirt.

194
00:10:06,430 --> 00:10:09,520
Oh, yeah. Ha, ha.

195
00:10:09,690 --> 00:10:14,320
So, um, did you have a nickname for me?

196
00:10:09,690 --> 00:10:14,320
Uh, no. No.

197
00:10:14,480 --> 00:10:16,400
Yes, you did. What was it?

198
00:10:16,610 --> 00:10:19,200
Um, it's...

199
00:10:19,360 --> 00:10:20,860
Cutie McPretty.

200
00:10:21,030 --> 00:10:24,870
Oh, that's so sweet.

201
00:10:25,040 --> 00:10:28,370
Listen, I gotta tell you, I'm having a great time.

202
00:10:28,580 --> 00:10:32,500
You know how you said it might be weird, the whole student-teacher thing?

203
00:10:32,670 --> 00:10:38,010
And to be frank, I thought it would be too. But it's not. I mean, it's not at all.

204
00:10:42,050 --> 00:10:44,430
Dr. Geller.

205
00:10:42,050 --> 00:10:44,430
Burt.

206
00:10:47,430 --> 00:10:49,270
So did you sleep well last night?

207
00:10:49,440 --> 00:10:50,480
I did.

208
00:10:49,440 --> 00:10:50,480
Yeah?

209
00:10:50,650 --> 00:10:53,980
I did. Monica was so sweet. She left a little mint on my pillow.

210
00:10:54,570 --> 00:10:56,480
Know what Joey left on my pillow?

211
00:10:54,570 --> 00:10:56,480
What?

212
00:10:56,650 --> 00:10:57,860
Gum.

213
00:10:58,530 --> 00:11:01,340
Well, we determined the cause of the fire.

214
00:11:01,340 --> 00:11:04,280
Yeah, I know. It was my candle, my candle.

215
00:11:04,830 --> 00:11:07,200
No, there was an appliance left on in the bathroom.

216
00:11:07,370 --> 00:11:08,870
It looks like a curling iron.

217
00:11:09,040 --> 00:11:11,540
I don't use a curling iron.

218
00:11:09,040 --> 00:11:11,540
Well, someone does.

219
00:11:12,580 --> 00:11:15,670
Don't look at me, my hair's straight. Straight, straight, straight.

220
00:11:16,630 --> 00:11:19,550
It could've been a hair-straightener.

221
00:11:16,630 --> 00:11:19,550
Oh.

222
00:11:21,550 --> 00:11:24,090
This is where I keep the pizza.

223
00:11:24,510 --> 00:11:27,140
And... Hey, where'd the napkin go?

224
00:11:35,110 --> 00:11:38,070
There you go. I wouldn't want my best guest to strain her eyes.

225
00:11:38,230 --> 00:11:40,860
Thanks, Monica.

226
00:11:41,030 --> 00:11:43,700
Does that smell bother you?

227
00:11:41,030 --> 00:11:43,700
What, the smell from Joey's?

228
00:11:43,860 --> 00:11:45,740
No, I can hardly smell it over here.

229
00:11:46,700 --> 00:11:50,910
Well, you let me know if you can. Because I can bake a pie to cover it.

230
00:11:52,210 --> 00:11:54,920
I can smell it a little. Bake the pie.

231
00:11:52,210 --> 00:11:54,920
Okay.

232
00:11:59,210 --> 00:12:00,420
Hello?

233
00:12:00,590 --> 00:12:03,470
Oh, yes, one minute, please. It's for you. It's the fire inspector.

234
00:12:03,630 --> 00:12:07,640
Oh. Hello? Yeah, this is Phoebe.

235
00:12:07,810 --> 00:12:08,850
Really?

236
00:12:09,010 --> 00:12:12,810
Yeah, so it turns out that it wasn't the hair-straightener...

237
00:12:12,980 --> 00:12:14,890
that started the fire.

238
00:12:15,060 --> 00:12:17,400
No, no. It was the candles.

239
00:12:17,570 --> 00:12:21,070
Yeah. It's very not good leaving candles unattended.

240
00:12:21,240 --> 00:12:25,910
In fact, one of the first things they teach you in fire school is...

241
00:12:26,120 --> 00:12:27,410
Uh...

242
00:12:30,200 --> 00:12:32,410
Uh, okay, well, I have to go now.

243
00:12:37,590 --> 00:12:40,380
We had such a great time. She's incredible.

244
00:12:40,550 --> 00:12:43,550
I thought the age difference might be a problem, but it wasn't.

245
00:12:43,720 --> 00:12:46,930
It wasn't at all. Elizabeth is very mature for her age.

246
00:12:51,680 --> 00:12:54,680
A concept lost on some people.

247
00:12:54,890 --> 00:12:56,520
So it's okay to date a student?

248
00:12:56,690 --> 00:12:57,850
Well, not really.

249
00:12:58,020 --> 00:13:00,770
I mean, technically, it's not against the rules or anything.

250
00:13:00,940 --> 00:13:02,190
But it is frowned upon...

251
00:13:02,360 --> 00:13:04,860
especially by that professor we ran into last night.

252
00:13:05,030 --> 00:13:06,950
Judgy von Holier-Than-Thou.

253
00:13:10,030 --> 00:13:11,080
Just be careful, okay?

254
00:13:11,240 --> 00:13:15,000
You don't wanna get a reputation as Professor McNails-His-Students. Ha, ha.

255
00:13:17,960 --> 00:13:21,380
Yeah. What should I do?

256
00:13:17,960 --> 00:13:21,380
Well, Ross, it seems pretty clear.

257
